import collections,json,re
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
read=lambda n:json.loads((p/n).read_text())
pub=read('publication.json');m=read('metadata.json');profit=read('profitability.json');sizes=read('artifact-sizes.json')['bytes'];audit=read('root-interval-verification.json');imp=read('observation-import.json');route=read('backend-routing.json');test=re.search(r'Ran (\d+) tests in ([\d.]+)s\s+OK\s*$',(p/'knowledge-tests.log').read_text());assert test
fmt=lambda ci:f'{ci[0]:.3f}× [{ci[1]:.3f}, {ci[2]:.3f}]'
lines=['# Ink web proof batch 10 — 10 October 2026','',f'Two proof authors and an independent reviewer supplied **{pub["added_entries"]} fresh checked proofs**, growing the database **{pub["previous_entries"]}→{pub["entries"]}**. All **{test[1]} knowledge tests pass** in {test[2]} seconds. Six U32 representatives are measured with the same frozen compiler and complete calls, alongside original-algorithm JavaScript/Rust-Wasm controls.','',
'| Proof family | Instances | Transformation |','|---|---:|---|','| Cubic/quartic/quintic second differences | 9 | `(x+k)^n-2*x^n+(x-k)^n` becomes a smaller exact polynomial |','| Nested left zip and postmap | 4 | Nested same-source zip stages become one map, preserving arithmetic order |','| Nested right zip and postmap | 4 | Right nested zip stages become one map, preserving arithmetic order |','| Two mapped lists, multiplicative zip, postmap | 4 | All stages become one map with the same per-element callback expressions/product/postmap |','',
'The finite-difference laws cover U32/I32/U64 wrapping rings modulo 2^32 or 2^64. They are word computations, with no floating-point derivative/accuracy claim. Targets are `6*x*k*k`, `2*k*k*(6*x*x+k*k)` and `10*x*k*k*(2*x*x+k*k)`; the same final calibration offset is retained. Timed representative outputs remain input-dependent at steps 7/-3. Collection laws also cover F32 and preserve exact source operation grouping and exceptional-value behavior. Their callbacks are pure and total in the modeled semantics; no effectful callback elimination is asserted.','',
'All typed laws admit, default-select, replay and reify. Old914 applies zero laws to the actual benchmark sources and retains all six original bodies. The new default selection applies one fresh law per kernel. [Author evidence](../../knowledge/research/web-stack-proofs-10/), [publication](publication.json), [full tests](knowledge-tests.log) and [independent review](../../knowledge/research/web-stack-proofs-10/review.md) preserve receipts and false controls. Typed correctness coverage is broader than the U32 timing scope.','',
f'Prior snapshot `{pub["previous_snapshot"]}`; new snapshot `{pub["snapshot"]}`; compiler `{pub["compiler_sha256"]}`. [Metadata](metadata.json) freezes {len(m["artifact_hashes"])} artifacts. All 102 guarded compiler/core/runtime/planner/backend source hashes remain unchanged. Generated functions trust callers; no validators or optional checking wrappers are added.','',
'Thirteen correctness inputs include empty/singleton, U32 boundaries, zero/unit factors and random words. Timed shapes combine small/full-width words with lengths 32/4096/65536, offsets 509/0x9e3779b9 and steps 7/2^32-3. No artificial repeat loops are added. Independent Python unbounded even-binomial expansion/collection closed forms check complete outputs; literal wrapping operations/stages corroborate all boundary words and the first four other words. Original numeric controls preserve exact source AST association; collection controls preserve all original stages. Normal JIT/release optimizations are allowed.','',
'Complete calls include exactly one full typed-input snapshot, applicable Wasm input copies/public output conversion, await and checksum consumption. GPU includes actual upload, dispatch and readback. Startup and first calls are separate. Rust reuses final input/output storage; intermediate Vec stages receive ordinary release optimization. These control/boundary choices limit cross-language comparisons. Expert already-factored/fused controls, native Rust and general language rankings are outside scope.','',
'Control preflight passes 78 original-JS complete outputs and 276 Python literal values; CPU prevalidation passes 858 exact comparisons. Seven shuffled paired rounds follow calibration/discarded warmup. No compiler/test/analysis jobs run during sequential Node/browser timing. Individual 95% paired intervals are exploratory and unadjusted for multiplicity; correlated runtime/direct views are not independent replications.','',
'Largest full-width browser prior/new complete-call ratios (above 1 favors new proofs):','',
'| Kernel | Runtime JS | Wasm | Comparable actual GPU |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for row in read('browser-summary.json')['measurements']:
 if row['input']=='full-65536':
  r=row['paired_ratios_95pct'];lines.append(f'| {row["case"]} | {fmt(r["prior_over_checked_js"])} | {fmt(r["prior_over_checked_wasm"])} | '+(fmt(r['prior_over_checked_gpu']) if 'prior_over_checked_gpu' in r else 'Prior fallback; checked shader eligible')+' |')
counts={b:dict(collections.Counter(d['verdict'] for d in profit['decisions'] if d['backend']==b)) for b in ['js','direct_js','wasm','gpu']}
lines+=['',f'[Profitability profiles](profitability.json): **{profit["counts"]}**; per backend {counts}. Unsupported/adverse comparisons recommend retaining the prior candidate. This does not implement automatic target selection. All adverse comparisons are retained:','', '| Host | Kernel/input | Backend | Prior/new interval |','|---|---|---|---:|']
if not any(d['verdict']=='slower' for d in profit['decisions']):lines.append('| — | No supported adverse cells in the main run | — | — |')
for d in profit['decisions']:
 if d['verdict']=='slower':lines.append(f'| {d["host"]} | {d["case"]}/{d["input"]} | {d["backend"]} | {fmt(d["ratio_95pct"])} |')
lines+=['',f'Actual WebGPU has **{audit["actual_gpu_variant_cells"]} variant/cells and {audit["gpu_timed_samples"]} timed samples**; {audit["gpu_fallback_variant_cells"]} fallback records remain excluded. Each actual vector call reports one dispatch, `4*N+24` upload bytes and `4*N` readback bytes. Three original collection pipelines have unsupported nested receivers; new direct maps become shader-eligible. Eligibility alone provides no prior/new GPU speed ratio.','',
f'[Routing evidence](backend-routing.json) records {route["paired_comparisons"]} current CPU/GPU intervals. Fastest checked-backend median counts: {dict(collections.Counter(x["lowest_median_current_backend"] for x in route["cells"]))}. GPU-resident pipelines and automatic routing are unmeasured/unimplemented.','',
'Uncompressed emitted sizes:','', '| Artifact | Old914 | Checked | Reduction |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for name in ['program.mjs','cpu.c','cpu.wasm']:
 a,b=sizes['prior'][name],sizes['checked'][name];lines.append(f'| {name} | {a} | {b} | {(1-b/a)*100:.1f}% |')
lines+=['','Plans/runtime/compressed transfer are excluded. Shader count changes 3→6, so aggregate WGSL size is not like-for-like.','',f'Importing **{imp["imported"]} authenticated Wasm observations** grows canonical observations **{imp["before"]}→{imp["after"]}**, preserving the proof pin. Memory means exported Wasm linear-memory highwater only; host/JS/GPU memory is unmeasured, so latency/counter data remains archived without invented memory records. [Import receipt](observation-import.json) records identities and source hashes.','']
for host in ['node','browser']:
 s=read(f'{host}-summary.json');lines.append(f'[{host.title()} report]({host}-REPORT.md): {s["samples"]} timed samples, {s["validation"]["comparisons"]} exact comparisons and {s["observations"]} observations. Raw trials, warmups, calibration, checksums, nonmutation and fallback reasons are archived.')
lines+=['',f'[Independent interval audit](root-interval-verification.json) recomputes {audit["intervals_recomputed"]} intervals. [Final verification](verification.json) authenticates all members, frozen artifacts, guarded source files and imported observations. Everything remains local; no commit, push or PR is created.','']
if (p/'gpu-confirmation.json').exists():
 c=read('gpu-confirmation.json');lines+=['Independent GPU confirmation: '+c['conclusion']+' '+c['input_scope']+' [Receipt](gpu-confirmation.json) and [separate report](../web-stack-proofs-10-gpu-confirmation-2026-10-10/browser-REPORT.md) retain the repeat. No timings are pooled and no repeat observations are imported.','']
else:lines+=['No independently confirmed GPU performance gain is claimed.','']
(p/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));print('report written')
